rrent state:\n- `src/unit.ts` → `export const unit = 21;`\n- `src/double.ts` → imports `./unit.ts`, `double()` returns `21 * 2 = 42`\n- `test/long.test.ts` → asserts `double() === 42`, prints `LONG_SESSION_OK` on success\n\nThe test file was not modified; `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and all other files remain untouched.\nCreated files:\n\n**`src/unit.ts`** (new; also created the `src/` directory it needed)\n```ts\nexport const unit = 21;\n```\n\n**`src/double.ts`** (new)\n```ts\nimport { unit } from \"./unit.ts\";\n\nexport function double(): number {\n  return unit * 2;\n}\n```\nSpecifier is `\"./unit.ts\"` rather than `\"./unit\"` because Node's native ESM/type-stripping requires an explicit extension for relative imports.\n\n**`test/long.test.ts`** (new; also created the `test/` directory)\n```ts\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { double } from \"../src/double.ts\";\n\ntest(\"double() equals 42\", () => {\n  assert.equal(double(), 42);\n  console.log(\"LONG_SESSION_OK\");\n});\n```\n\nRun: `node --test test/long.test.ts` → 1 test, 1 pass, 0 fail, exit code 0 (run twice, both green; no repairs needed).\n\nExact printed marker:\n\n```\nLONG_SESSION_OK\n```\n\n(In the TAP output it appears as the line `# LONG_SESSION_OK`, which is the runner prefixing captured stdout — the marker string itself is exactly `LONG_SESSION_OK`.)\n\nUntouched: `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`; no test runner or configuration added, and `test/oracle.test.ts` was neither created nor modified."
